  "explanation": "Both arms use the same 120 s RECENT window, so the 8 extra are NOT a window difference. They are a frame-SAMPLING-DENSITY difference: the device samples 37 frames across the 120 s window (mean stride 3.33 s) while cloud K3 samples 121 frames at ~1 fps. All 8 have answer intervals of only 1-2 s, and in every case a single device frame gap straddles the whole interval, so the evidence lies inside the window but between two sampled frames. evidence_covered is therefore a property of the ARM's frame budget, not of the question.",
